Process rules and the access log for the desktop tun inbound.

When keqdroid moved desktop TUN from sing-box to xray's own tun inbound, xray
had to take over what sing-box's process rules did. Three things were missing:

- "Only the selected apps" sends every other program direct. mihomo writes it
  as NOT(PROCESS-NAME-REGEX ...); xray has no NOT. An entry written as "!name"
  in a rule's process list now makes the rule match a process outside the
  "!" entries. A process the system tables do not know counts as outside, as
  for mihomo's NOT.
- Windows names and paths ignore case, and the path a file dialog returns can
  differ in case from the one the system reports. On Windows names, paths,
  folders and the .exe suffix now compare without case. The suffix is cut
  without case from the name the system reports too: xray cut only a
  lowercase .exe, and a rule for winword missed WINWORD.EXE.
- Each process rule searched the system tables again for the same connection,
  and the access log needs the program too. common/net.FindProcessCached keeps
  one result per source for 2 seconds. Not on Android: there the app keeps
  its own answers, by both ends of a connection, and keeps no failed one.

The access log ends with " process: <path>", so the app's Connections screen
can name the program as it did with sing-box: always for TUN connections, as
sing-box's find_process did there, and for local SOCKS and HTTP clients only
when the config has an outbound tagged keq-process-log (routed to by nothing),
as sing-box looked those up only in debug mode. Not on Android, where the app
asks the VPN service for connection owners.
